The fatal weakness is the missing ablation validating that safety constraints actually contribute. This directly questions the central contribution. Combined with overstated correctness guarantees and limited scope to only math/code benchmarks, this is a borderline-reject paper. The strong empirical table (13 baselines) prevents it from falling further, but missing the ablation on the core claim is ICLR-disqualifying without major revision.

