## Reasoning

**Compared to LAMDA (6.7):** LAMDA provides a comprehensive dataset contribution with a fairly straightforward methodology but has a fundamental confound (label drift vs. feature drift conflation). AUTO-RT has a more complex and novel methodology (RL + hierarchical strategy formulation), strong multi-model evaluation (18 models), and is directly addressing the very relevant LLM safety challenge. However, AUTO-RT has a missing limitations section, unclear computational cost, and reproducibility gaps in downgrade model construction — issues comparable in severity to LAMDA's weaknesses. I place AUTO-RT roughly at or slightly below LAMDA.

