CMIC sits comfortably above the borderline-accept range (6.0). It is on par with QVGen (6.8) in rigor and empirical quality, but slightly narrower in scope and less generalizable. It falls short of the PGM paper (7.0) in terms of paradigm-level novelty. The weaknesses (non-differentiable CTP, unexplored entropy model question) are minor and not deal-breaking. I assign a score of **6.6**.

