## Dimensional Comparison

### Novelty
ARSS is the first to apply GPT-style decoder-only autoregressive models to novel view synthesis with explicit camera control — a genuine first-mover contribution in an active area (world models, NVS). However, the novelty is mostly in the *application* of existing techniques (video tokenizer from Tang et al., spatial token permutation from Pang et al./Yu et al., Plücker ray camera conditioning) rather than introducing fundamentally new algorithmic ideas. This is similar to **jigsaw3d** (adapts 2D patch shuffling to 3D) or **flashmono** (adapts feed-forward prediction to SLAM). Both better than anyavatar's incremental extension but less novel than partition_generative_modeling or qvgen which introduce conceptually new mechanisms.

### Technical Soundness
A critical gap exists: the camera autoencoder — arguably the most novel component — has no ablation study. The spatial token permutation strategy and training objective are described ambiguously (incomplete Eq. 7 noted). This echoes **dens3r**'s incomplete ablation and reproducibility concerns. The video tokenizer and camera conditioning choices are reasonable but lack thorough justification. Weaker than qvgen (thorough ablations, theoretical motivation) or condition_errors (theoretical analysis despite assumptions).

### Empirical Support
Experiments span three datasets (RealEstate10K, ACID, DL3DV) and include zero-shot generalization, which is commendable. However, ARSS only achieves *comparable* (not superior) performance to SOTA diffusion methods — winning on some metrics (PSNR, LPIPS) while losing on others (SSIM, FID). This is weaker than flashmono (clear 10× speedup advantage) or qvgen (clear SOTA gains). The error accumulation analysis is a genuine and novel empirical insight supporting the method's applicability to long trajectories.

### Significance
The application of causal AR models to NVS has real significance for long-trajectory world modeling. The error-accumulation advantage offers practical motivations. But the lack of a clear performance advantage over diffusion baselines limits the immediate impact. This is similar to anyavatar (novel application, clear practical limitations) or dens3r (moderate novelty, high downstream significance).

### Clarity
Method descriptions have noted ambiguities (incomplete equations, unclear permutation mechanics), which limits reproducibility. Similar to dens3r and jigsaw3d. Better than condition_errors in terms of high-level structure, worse in terms of completeness of equations.

