The paper is substantially better than the 0–1.0 range papers (it has real experiments, genuine ML grounding, and a truly novel conceptual contribution). It is also clearly below the 7.5–8.0 range papers: those papers had rigorous mathematical proofs, validated their methods on real-world datasets, and provided efficient algorithms. The forgetting paper offers a conceptual framework with small-scale validation and no comparisons to existing metrics—a profile more consistent with borderline territory.

The closest comparable is a hypothetical combination of the "beyond_turing" conceptual novelty (elevated) with some empirical grounding (closer to the 3.3 papers). The breadth of paradigm coverage (5 domains) partially compensates for the limited scale within each, but the missing sensitivity analysis and metric comparisons remain significant omissions for ICLR.

